comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T22:10:16.764Z",codex-sol,"Restart by codex-sol: preserved remote PR #118 and all existing bot replies/reactions were inspected. Branch is already current with origin/main. No new actionable unresolved inline finding is present. Retain documented coverage/health/publication blockers; rerun unchanged full CI gate with the host-wide flock. No merge, publish or item closure."
  "2026-10-02T22:25:27.456Z",codex-sol,"Restart: locked npm ci and release:check pass 196/196 tests, zero skips, configured 100% lines/branches/functions over three sources, without a separate statements dimension. The PM-linked seven-test real prepare-launcher suite passes both malformed package states. Strict health with merge drivers and tracked build output equality pass. The prior run-callback migration fix and f4dea28 broken-install regressions remain unchanged. Whole-source coverage pm-starter-puy5, existing public-history/publication privacy blocker pm-starter-asud, and substantive final-head reviews remain open. No merge, publish or close; release claim for orchestrator."
  "2026-10-02T22:48:42.926Z",codex-sol,"Review round clarification: pm-starter-puy5 now explicitly requires statement-reporting instrumentation before four-metric acceptance. Current release:check 196/196 passes with three reported metrics over three files; coverage/privacy blockers remain. Release claim for orchestrator."
  "2026-10-04T11:19:19.387Z",codex-sol,"Isolated worktree from origin/main a0bf60e. Consolidate Dependabot #117 #120 #121 including exact CodeQL SHA, PM CLI/pm-ops/pm-changelog 2026.10.4 pins and current exact dev pins. Preserve peer/manifest floor. No open security alerts. Full locked CI gate and real-tracker packed npm/native Bun main commands plus read-only managed GitHub preview planned. Existing coverage completeness and statement debt remains tracked in pm-starter-puy5; no narrowed or lowered gate."
  "2026-10-04T11:34:35.044Z",codex-sol,"Real-data packed starter demo correctly refused a default-budget partial list (4 of 71 items); six-large-body regression reproduced silent field compaction under the default read. Test-first fix switches the shared reader to canonical pm list --all --full --include-body --no-truncate --strict-read --json, preserving receipt refusals. New regression now passes; 107 command tests pass with zero skips. Re-run full gate and both packed runtimes; verify these flags against the declared 2026.8.15 floor before retaining it."
  "2026-10-04T11:41:46.731Z",codex-sol,"Floor verification found 2026.8.15 supports --status all, --full, --include-body, --no-truncate and --strict-read, but lacks --all. Use canonical list --status all instead, which works on both the declared floor and current CLI. This keeps the existing peer/manifest floor without adding unsupported options."
  "2026-10-04T11:54:39.351Z",codex-sol,"Review follow-up: Greptile pm-slack#124 finding 4177259636 correctly flags privileged Windows directory symlink creation. Shared dangling-link fixture now requests a junction on Windows and a directory link on POSIX without adding skips. Targeted launcher suite passes 9/9 on this Linux host; native Windows execution is unverified. Canonical launcher bytes and production behavior are unchanged. Initial substantive review remains unavailable from CodeRabbit automatic-skip/Sourcery quota and silent reviewers; request one explicit re-review after this push, retain open readiness boundary."
  "2026-10-04T12:03:17.068Z",codex-sol,"CI identity audit correctly rejected an absolute home path in captured dogfood output. Rewrote only this feature branch commits to use a HOME placeholder in public evidence; no gate lowered or ignored. CodeRabbit finding 4177439569 is valid: updated the two acceptance version targets from 2026.9.29 to 2026.10.4, preserving every other completion check. Revalidate committed branch identity scope and final CI. Repository-wide public-history privacy and full PM-linked gate prerequisites remain separately open."
  "2026-10-04T12:09:22.904Z",codex-sol,"Greptile finding 4177448264 verified against both recorded dogfood outputs: keyword search returned coverage issue pm-starter-puy5, not the certification item. Corrected evidence summary, actual_result and PR body to name the actual result. Existing raw npm/native Bun output is the validation oracle; no executable change or new test needed. CI history audit now passes after public receipt path sanitization; full-repository historical privacy and independent coverage debt remain open."
  "2026-10-04T12:15:33.539Z",codex-sol,"Full PM-linked release gate verified after review fixes: npx pm test pm-starter-cz6b --only-index 3 --run --progress --workspace-context source --override-linked-workspace-context --pm-context tracker --override-linked-pm-context PASS (linked command holds flock heavy-gate.lock); 200/200 tests, zero skips, unchanged configured 3-source coverage, audits/pack/changelog/attestation pass. Snapshot/none attempt failed because Git metadata is excluded; source/none was refused by CLI policy. Explicit tracker/source mode succeeds with 71 copied tracker items and no context mismatch. Result tracking is disabled by existing repo policy, so outcomes are recorded here and in actual_result/documentation; policy unchanged. Final exact-head CI/review remains separate."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T14:50:00.484Z",codex,"2026-09-29 baseline on main head 27941da: direct npm run release:check passed with installed CLI SDK, pm-ops and pm-changelog 2026.9.23, zero production audit findings and changelog parity. npm registry now publishes CLI SDK and pm-ops 2026.9.29 and pm-changelog 2026.9.25. Candidate exact-pins those three in package and lockfile; scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts is copied byte-for-byte from the published pm-ops 2026.9.29 template and npm run prepare passed. Current CLI binary reports 2026.9.29. Full new-pin gate, packed npm/Bun behavior and remote review still pending. Existing privacy issue pm-starter-asud and release-auth/order issues remain independent blockers."
  "2026-09-29T15:02:07.460Z",codex,"2026-09-29 red-green packed acceptance: the original packed candidate on published CLI 2026.9.29 installed and ran starter greet/summary in a real npm project, but strict health failed extension_migration_pending for pm-starter-0001-noop; pm package migrate returned ok=true with pending_count=1 and no receipt. Inspecting published SDK types showed SchemaMigrationDefinition.run is the executable hook; package source incorrectly used up. A focused test expecting run failed with TypeError, then passed after changing the callback to run. Repacked candidate SHA-256 03dc3688497cdb88ed007fbaafed414191dc3b8c68754ed31fa284e6460ac45e. Fresh npm/npx and Bun/bunx projects on CLI 2026.9.29 installed it, created one real task, invoked starter greet and summary, auto-applied the demo migration, and passed strict PM health with zero warnings. Explicit package migrate then reported skipped_count=1 with before=applied in each project. Direct and PM-linked npm run release:check passed 195/195 tests, zero skips, 6 docstring files/32 declarations, configured 100% lines/branches/functions across 3 sources, zero production audit, pack/changelog/attestation. Statement coverage and three authored executable scripts are outside that claim under pm-starter-puy5. Public-history privacy and release-auth/order issues remain open; no publication or merge approval is claimed."
  "2026-09-29T15:12:34.607Z",codex,"Greptile P2 on PR #118 at head d4d62e0 found missing launcher fixtures for a dangling pm-ops link and a directory lacking package.json. Added both real child-process checkout cases to the existing test and confirmed 7/7 focused tests pass, with nonzero failure and no registered drivers for either broken state. Full release gate is running before the review-fix push."
  "2026-09-29T15:13:12.727Z",codex,"Review-fix precommit full release gate passed: 196/196 tests, zero skips, configured three-source coverage thresholds, zero production audit findings, pack/changelog/attestation. Greptile inline P2 was positively reacted to and answered with exact fixture assertions. This does not close the all-source coverage or historical privacy blockers."
